  "rationale": "The workflow is Bazel-heavy (bazelisk test/build in TFLite, ARM, and MLIR jobs) but runs every Bazel invocation on a fresh runner with no persistent Bazel action cache, so unchanged inputs are recompiled/retested repeatedly. P-LIT-BAZEL-INCREMENTAL (cache Bazel build results) is supported evidence: existing Bazel build, and Bazel's disk cache is input-keyed/content-addressed, so restored entries are only reused when inputs match and stale entries are simply rebuilt, preserving all test targets and coverage. I added an actions/cache@v6 step (already used elsewhere in this workflow) for ~/.cache/bazel and a --disk_cache=~/.cache/bazel/disk_cache entry in .bazelrc.user for the three Bazel jobs. No test commands, targets, filters, secrets, permissions, or deployment steps were changed.",
